    "title": "The Unopened Box",
    "passage": "Mia brought a box of drawing things when she visited Tom. She had planned to teach him how to draw a horse. Tom met her at the door holding a page covered in tiny buildings. He began showing her the shops, park, and school in his paper town. Mia kept her box closed while he talked. When he pointed to an empty field, she asked what belonged there. Tom said he had not decided yet. Mia opened her box and drew a horse on a fresh piece of paper. Tom placed it in the field and drew a path leading to the town. They spent the afternoon adding animals and places for them to live. On her way home, Mia saw she had never given her drawing lesson. Her horse had found somewhere to live instead.",
